  "reverse": [
    { "id": "US5.5", "status": "N/A", "target": "Undo is required by three artifacts and defined by no requirement: AC5.3.3 exercises it, team-practices.md names it as one of five editing actions in the merge gate, and wireframes.md's Success state promises it after a corridor apply. FR4.1 and FR4.2 are the nearest upstream but neither mentions reversal. Raised for a requirements amendment alongside OQ-US1." },
    { "id": "US7.5", "status": "N/A", "target": "FR6.4 permits correcting imported data; it says nothing about what happens to a correction when the street is imported again. The three-outcome behaviour (fingerprint match, key resolves, unresolved) is derived from the osm2streets data model rather than from a requirement." },
    { "id": "US8.2", "status": "N/A", "target": "Derived from the Q6/Q9 browser-first persistence decision rather than from a requirement ID. FR7.2 requires a pre-sign-in design to survive signing in; it does not cover the case where device storage lost it. Raised for a requirements amendment alongside OQ-US1." },
    { "id": "US8.3", "status": "N/A", "target": "Derived from the Q9 opt-in-upload decision, and raised to Must Have at the mob triage (Q12). No FR covers a deliberate upload without an account; FR7.2 and FR9.3 both assume the account path. Covered by OQ-US1." },
